      "structuredReports": [
        {
          "seq": 145,
          "time": 1792571865938,
          "status": "ready",
          "summary": "Implemented complete dependency-free Node.js ESM order, inventory, and payment CLI with the following structure:\n\n**cli.mjs**: Main CLI entry point that:\n- Parses commands from arguments\n- Loads store and builds state from events\n- Executes command handlers\n- Commits new events atomically with failpoint support\n- Outputs JSON results or exits with errors\n\n**lib/command.mjs**: Command parser with validation for:\n- Identifiers (SKU, ID, KEY matching ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9-]{0,15}$)\n- Stock (0-1,000,000)\n- Price (1-1,000,000,000 cents)\n- Quantities (positive without leading zeros)\n\n**lib/storage.mjs**: Atomic storage layer:\n- Loads and validates store structure and event sequences\n- Saves via temp file + atomic rename\n- Returns empty store for missing files\n- Rejects corruption without overwriting\n\n**lib/state.mjs**: Event sourcing with replay:\n- Builds current state from event log\n- Tracks products (stock, reserved, price)\n- Tracks orders (status, payment)\n- Tracks payment keys for idempotency\n- Maintains creation order for products and orders\n\n**lib/handlers.mjs**: Command handlers implementing:\n- Product add/list with reservation tracking\n- Order create/get/list with availability checks\n- Payment with idempotency (declined/approved)\n- Cancellation with idempotency (reserved→cancelled, paid→refunded)\n- Audit returning {seq, type, id} events\n\nAll contract requirements implemented: inventory management, order reservation, payment idempotency with historical responses, cancellation/refund, event replay, atomic commits, and failpoint simulation."
        }
      ],
